# Delivery (Fluent Mobile)

## Never push to `main`

**Agents must not** commit, push, or merge directly to `main` (or the default branch).

Every change — including infra, CI, docs, Dependabot follow-ups, and `expo install --fix` — goes through:

1. **Ticket on Project 4** — GitHub Issue `#NNN` **on** the [Fluent Mobile Board](https://github.com/orgs/eten-tech-foundation/projects/4/views/9) (org project #4, view 9). Ask if missing — except explicit **no-ticket chores** approved in-session (`Refs: none`). See [docs/issue-tracking.md](../../docs/issue-tracking.md). Board Status/Priority edits: [docs/guides/project-board.md](../../docs/guides/project-board.md) and [project-board.mdc](./project-board.mdc).
2. **Feature branch** — `{author}/{type}/{issue-number}-{slug}` (see `/create-pr-branch` or `/start-issue`); no-ticket chores may use `{author}/chore/{slug}` without an issue number.
3. **Pull request** — title `[#NNN]: Description` (or plain title for no-ticket chores); body filled from [`.cursor/templates/pr-template.md`](../templates/pr-template.md) (mandatory — do not substitute a short Summary/Test plan); `Refs #NNN` **or** `Refs: none` under Details (never `Closes` / `Fixes` / `Resolves`); assign the PR to the author; set Project 4 to **In PR Review** when there is a ticket. Procedure: [`.claude/commands/create-pr.md`](../../.claude/commands/create-pr.md) (`/open-pr` alias).
4. **Human merge** — agents push **feature branches only**; never merge unless the user explicitly asks for a Dependabot squash merge in that session. **Needs QA?** per [docs/guides/qa-process.md](../../docs/guides/qa-process.md) — QA is post-merge on the nightly; engineering-only (`Needs QA? No`) → automation sets **Done** and closes the linked issue. Never use closing keywords in the PR body.

Allowed on `main` locally: `git checkout main`, `git pull`, read-only validation. **Not allowed:** `git push origin main`, commits on `main`, or opening PRs with `main` as the head branch.

## PR body

Fill [`.cursor/templates/pr-template.md`](../templates/pr-template.md) on every agent-opened PR. Section requirements and Needs QA checkboxes live in that template and in `/create-pr`. Keep under ~400 lines; no nested fenced code blocks. This template wins over org-wide PR body shapes.

## Dependabot exception (merge only)

When the user asks to **handle/process Dependabot PRs**, agents may approve and squash-merge **existing** Dependabot PR branches into `main` per [dependabot-workflow.mdc](./dependabot-workflow.mdc). Agent-authored fixes still need a separate ticketed PR — never push those to `main`.

## Before delivery

1. Run local gates from [commands.mdc](./commands.mdc) (also listed in [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md)).
2. Apply delivery judgment from [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) (AC, scope, abstraction, human QA).
3. One independent `code-reviewer` pass on the final intended diff (proportional re-review — see [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) and [`.claude/commands/create-pr.md`](../../.claude/commands/create-pr.md)); fix or waive per-item before handoff.
4. Watch CI after push/open; report done only when required checks are green (or an out-of-scope base-branch blocker is documented).

Human merges — agents do not merge over unfixed review findings.
